The user provided a review with 3 findings. We need to fix F-01 (code + test), F-02 (AEBE stale counts/revision), F-03 (terminology). We should follow receiving-code-review: verify each, then implement. F-01 is valid: no-op path returns request.existing directly, aliasing/mutable. Need to change adapter to always call Core admission, even with empty candidates, and freeze the emission. Need to consider: `registerOrphanAssessments([], graph, existing)` will:
- check graph provenance
- validate no candidates
- `admitAssessments(existing, [])`:
  - check arrays
  - validateNoSelfSupersession([]) ok
  - deepCopy(existing) → copy; deepFreeze → base
  - collectAssessmentIds(base, []) → checks duplicate IDs in existing; returns allIds
  - validateSupersessionTargets([], allIds) ok
  - build links; validateNoSupersessionCycles([], links) ok
  - return Object.freeze([...base]) → new frozen array, deep-frozen members.
So calling Core with empty candidates returns a new frozen copy. Good. Then adapter should return `assessments: []` (frozen?) and `registered: admitted.value`. Also freeze the emission object itself: `Object.freeze({ assessments, registered })`.

